+## 17. X2 task T3: match highlight, help overlay, selection kept across filter edits
+
+Part C replaces K9: the TUI now keeps the selected destination across filter edits. The K9 statements in §4 and
+§12 describe the earlier behaviour.
+
+- **All behaviour stays in `ListModel`** (`src/list_model.rs`); `tui.rs` only renders it.
+  - **Part C:** `refilter` remembers the selected destination (its index in the profile) before the edit. It
+    selects that destination again if it is still shown, else the first shown row. Leaving filter mode with
+    `Enter` does not refilter, so it keeps the selection.
+  - **Scrolling:** the model now owns the scroll offset. The renderer reports the list height with
+    `set_viewport` before each frame. The window is always full when there are enough rows, holds the selection,
+    and scrolls as little as possible. After a filter edit the selected row keeps its screen row where the list
+    allows. ratatui's own offset logic does not fill the window backwards, so the offset is set explicitly in
+    `ListState`.
+  - **Part A:** `find_ci` uses the filter's matching rule (`str::to_lowercase` + substring) and maps the match
+    back onto the original characters. `row_segments` splits a row into segments and underlines the first
+    match in the alias and, on rows of 50 columns or more, in the host. The renderer turns the underlined
+    segments into `Modifier::UNDERLINED` spans (SGR 4/24, no colour), so the underline is also shown under
+    `NO_COLOR`.
+  - **Part B:** `?` outside filter mode sets `help`. While it is set, only `?`/`Esc` (close) and `Ctrl-C`
+    (cancel) do anything. The overlay covers the whole screen, one `HELP_LINES` entry per row from the top, so
+    no list text shares a row with a help line. It is clipped on small terminals.
+- **Tests:**
+  - **Unit:** the K9 test is replaced by `filter_edit_keeps_selected_destination` and
+    `filter_edit_keeps_far_selection_visible_with_full_window`. New tests: `help_overlay`,
+    `find_ci_maps_to_original_text`, `row_segments_underline_first_match_in_alias_and_host` and
+    `model_row_uses_current_filter`.
+  - **pty (`tests/pty_tui.py`):** the VT model tracks underline per cell. The case
+    `k9-filter-edit-resets-selection` is replaced by `c-filter-edit-keeps-selection`. New cases:
+    `c-far-selection-stays-visible`, `a-underline-filter-match` and `b-help-overlay`.
+- **Harness 2.4.2:** `tui.filter_edit_resets_selection`, `tui.no_color` (last step) and
+  `tui.large_100_filter_latency` (update predicate) encode K9, so they are expected to fail.
